# meta-deploy.list: the queue meta-deploy.bash runs, in this order.
#
# STANDING RULE (CLAUDE/AgentNotes.md): this list is exactly what needs running NOW. Add a
# run when it is pending, remove it once it has run and is done, leave out what cannot
# usefully run yet, then ask the owner to run meta-deploy.bash. Every step a run needs lives
# in the plan's own scripts, so this is the only command the owner is handed. The order is by
# dependency. A plan with none of triage.bash, deploy.bash and acceptance.bash has nothing
# for the script to do. A triage-only plan is run once, read-only. Words after the folder
# name are passed to that plan's triage.bash, both runs.
#
# One entry per line, four kinds:
#   <plan folder>                  its triage, deploy and acceptance scripts, in order
#   playbooks/<path>.yml           a change no plan owns; run as one unit through its own
#                                  shebang, which goes through run.bash, exactly as
#                                  ./playbooks/imports/<play>.yml does by hand
#   <plan folder>/<script>.bash    one plan script, for a step none of the three fixed names
#                                  fits; run as one unit, like a playbook entry, except
#                                  that a script named *acceptance*.bash may exit 2 for
#                                  COULD NOT ESTABLISH, as an acceptance.bash may
#   changed-plays                  every play that has run here and has to run again, as
#                                  one unit: the checkout's ./run.bash --changed --yes, in
#                                  playbook-main.yml order, stopping at the first failure
#
# changed-plays runs WHERE IT STANDS in the list, like every other entry, and decides which
# plays it runs when it starts, so the entries above it have already run (a play an entry
# above ran is no longer changed, and is not run twice). Put it above the plan entries whose
# deploy or acceptance expects the changed plays to have run, which is the usual case, and
# below an entry it must follow. It replaces a hand-copied list of stale plays: name a
# playbooks/ entry only for a play that must run at a fixed point between two plan steps.
# Its description says which changed plays the agent expects it to pick up and why.
#
# A line starting with # is a comment and is the description of the entry below it: it is how
# the owner learns what a run will do, so write it. Blank lines are ignored. Any other line
# that is not an entry is a fatal error naming its line number.
# play-agent-bus.yml, the whole play (Plan 00201 Task 2.22): the agent-bus admin tool built from
# this checkout carries declare.py's pinned_tuwunel_version, the one reader of the Tuwunel pin
# (ccy-teams, the play's software digest and Plan 00161's probe all call it; a pin naming an
# empty version is now refused, as one naming none or two already was). The admin tool is part
# of the software digest, so the play reinstalls it on the host and applies each team again;
# nothing a user sees changes. Needs sudo once.
playbooks/imports/play-agent-bus.yml
# play-claude-yolo.yml, the whole play (Plan 00201 Task 2.22): the host's ccy becomes CCY
# 3.100.13 and the play builds container 2.79.8, whose image carries the same declare.py. It
# also rebuilds ~/.local/bin/ccy-teams and ccy-sessions from src-go, where the membership
# directory names and the remove's "homeserver down" message are now named constants that the
# plan checkers read instead of copying; their behaviour is unchanged. The next ccy launch
# rebuilds only a project's own image. Check after the run: `ccy --version` says 3.100.13, and a
# ccy session starts and attaches as before.
playbooks/imports/play-claude-yolo.yml
# Plan 00211 deploy 2 (Task 2.6), the reports and questions rooms, again (Plan 00201 Task 2.22).
# It passed on the host with the A3 join fix; it runs again because its checkers now read the
# values the product owns (the ccy session pingbus home, the team state directory, the inbox
# and consumed directory and dropped log names, the Element profile and accepted-seat paths)
# from this checkout instead of holding copies, and only a host run proves those reads. This runs deploy.bash --stage 2: it refuses unless the spike
# report says every fact holds, runs acceptance.bash --stage 1 as the pre-flight (an offline
# member is named, not judged), runs the whole play-agent-bus.yml and play-claude-yolo.yml
# (both run by the entries above, so they find little to change), then acceptance.bash --stage
# 2: it waits up to 180 s for every online coordinator to join its questions room and every
# running ccy seat its reports room, checks the rooms, adds and removes one throwaway worker
# that joins by one pingbus recv, must be refused the questions room and whose test report
# reaches no online inbox, posts a test report from an online LXC member (NOT JUDGED with
# none) and has the coordinator ask a test question (NOT JUDGED when it is offline). If A3
# says a seat beside Element was refused, run cc --teams once from a terminal, accept, and run
# this again. Needs sudo once. Afterwards, if the test question was asked, do the Element steps
# of the plan's ACCEPTANCE-owner.md.
00211-agent-bus-reports-and-questions-rooms/deploy-stage-2.bash
# Plan 00201 Task 2.7 (M7), the automated two-team acceptance, again (Task 2.22). It passed on
# the host with the image-build wait; it runs again because M7 checks now read the checkout
# seats directory, the agent-bus install-state, state and applied directories and the session
# records directory from this checkout product code instead of copying them. acceptance.bash only: it makes two throwaway teams declared in a
# run-directory host_vars (your host_vars and teams are never touched), runs one headless ccy
# session on both and a plain one (each one short turn on haiku), checks descriptions, launch
# block, per-session record, status line, `say` and SessionEnd, then purges both teams and
# checks their firewalld rules are gone, however the run ends. The first launch after the ccy
# play may sit through one project image build first, saying once a minute whose build it
# waits for (`ccy --build-lock` in another terminal shows or stops a hung one). Needs sudo
# once, ccy launched interactively in this checkout once (Quick Launch), and the hooks daemon
# installed.
00201-ccy-teams-many-teams-per-session-descriptions-and-a-picker
